  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Differentiate between communication and transmission. (3 marks)', 'Communication is the complete process of exchanging meaningful information between a sender and a receiver; it has five components - message, sender, receiver, medium and protocol - and succeeds only when the receiver understands the message (it can be two-way, with feedback). Transmission is the physical act of sending data as signals (electrical, light or radio) through a medium such as cable, fibre or air from one point to another; it is one part of communication and deals with signals, bandwidth, speed and transmission media rather than meaning.', null, '[{"point": "Communication: the whole process of exchanging meaningful information between a sender and receiver, involving message, sender, receiver, medium and protocol (understanding)", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Transmission: the physical sending of signals/ data over a medium from one point to another (one part of communication), concerned with signals, bandwidth and media", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
